An **export expression** tells NAHPU which record fields to output, what fixed
text to include around them, and how to handle missing or conditional values.
Expressions work in two places:

- text elements inside a [document template](../export-documents), such as a
  specimen label;
- `Custom field` columns inside a [record-export preset](../export-records).

The same expression produces the same text in both. For example,
`[taxonomy::genus] [taxonomy::specificEpithet]` {% ref id="C" /%} prints
`Rattus rattus` on a label and writes `Rattus rattus` to a spreadsheet cell.

## The basics in one minute

Wrap any field key in square brackets as `[table::field]`. Everything outside
brackets prints verbatim:

```text
Field no. [specimen::fieldNumber]
```

outputs `Field no. 156`. Three modifiers handle most formatting needs:

| Add | Purpose | Example | Output |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `??text` | Fallback when the field is empty | `[taxonomy::specificEpithet??sp.]` | `sp.` when no epithet is recorded |
| `#label` | Print a coded field's label instead of its integer code | `[mammalAttribute::testisPosition#label]` | `Scrotal` instead of `0` |
| `[[if]…]]` | Print text only when conditions hold | `[[if][coordinate::elevationInMeter!=""]=>"m"]]` | `m` only when elevation is recorded |

You rarely need to type keys manually: use `Insert Field` in the template
editor or `Add field` in a custom field column.

## Common expressions {% #common-expressions %}

Copy these into a document-template text element or into a tabular preset
column as noted. All examples below use specimen fields.

### Species name {% #species-name %}

```text
[taxonomy::genus] [taxonomy::specificEpithet]
```

Outputs `Rattus rattus`. For genus-only identifications, add a fallback so the
output reads `Rattus sp.`:

```text
[taxonomy::genus] [taxonomy::specificEpithet??sp.]
```

For the full scientific name including subspecies, use
`[specimen::scientificName]`. In a tabular preset, place either expression in a
`Custom field` column.

### Full locality {% #full-locality %}

Joins geography fields into one string while skipping empty parts, preventing
doubled commas when a level like county is blank:

```text
[geography::country]|[geography::islandGroup]|[geography::stateProvince]|[geography::county]|[geography::municipality]|[geography::locality]
```

Each `|` separates parts; the printed separator comes from the list settings:

- **Document template:** set `Text type` to `List Values` and choose the comma
  format.
- **Record-export preset:** set `Mapping type` to `List field`, `List output`
  to `One column`, and `Separator` to `Comma (A, B)`. Paste the expression into
  `Advanced` > `Raw source expression` and set `Column name (optional)`
  (required for Darwin Core and NAHPU namespace headers).

A complete record prints `Indonesia, West Java, Bogor, Cibodas`; one without a
county prints `Indonesia, West Java, Cibodas`. Add, remove, or reorder parts as
needed.

### Testis size {% #testis-size %}

Outputs `length x width` only when the testis is scrotal and both measurements
exist; otherwise outputs nothing:

```text
[[if][mammalAttribute::testisPosition=="0"&&mammalAttribute::testisLength!=""&&mammalAttribute::testisWidth!=""]=>"[mammalAttribute::testisLength] x [mammalAttribute::testisWidth]"]]
```

| Record | Output |
| --- | --- |
| Scrotal, 10 mm by 6.5 mm | `10 x 6.5` |
| Scrotal, width missing | Nothing |
| Abdominal | Nothing |
| Female | Nothing |

`"0"` is the stored code for Scrotal. Add ` mm` inside the quotes for a unit,
or add `|"not scrotal"` before `]]` to write an alternative for non-matching
records. See [Conditional text](#conditional-text). In a tabular preset, use a
`Custom field` column.

### Encoded field labels {% #encoded-labels %}

```text
[mammalAttribute::testisPosition#label]
```

Outputs `Scrotal` instead of the stored code `0`. Works in any text type,
including `Custom field` columns. See
[Decode an encoded field](#decode-an-encoded-field).

## Placeholders in detail

### Symbols

| Symbol | Meaning | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `[ ]` | Field placeholder | `[fieldNumber]` |
| `::` | Separates table from field in a full key | `[specimen::fieldNumber]` |
| `??` | Fallback when the field is empty | `[specimen::preparator??N/A]` |
| `#label` | Outputs a coded field's label instead of its code | `[mammalAttribute::testisPosition#label]` |
| `-img` | Renders a `.sex` field as an icon instead of text | `[mammal.sex]-img` |
| `[[ ]]` | Conditional expression | `[[specimen::condition][…]]` |
| `[[if]` … `]]` | Conditional text written only when conditions match | `[[if][…]=>" mm"]]` |

### Field keys

A placeholder accepts a full `table::field` key or a short field name:

```text
Field number: [specimen::fieldNumber]
Scientific name: [taxonomy::scientificName]
Locality: [site::specificLocality]
```

Use the full `table::field` key whenever two tables share a field name. The
field picker offers only fields available to the active record type.

### Missing values

`??` specifies what prints when a field is empty. The `No Content Placeholder`
setting writes this syntax for you:

| Option | Written as | Output when empty |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Blank` | `[specimen::preparator]` | Nothing |
| `table::field` | `[specimen::preparator??specimen::preparator]` | The field key as a visible reminder |
| `N/A` | `[specimen::preparator??N/A]` | `N/A` |
| `None` | `[specimen::preparator??None]` | `None` |
| Custom | `[specimen::preparator??not recorded]` | Your custom text |

Text after `??` prints verbatim. Placeholders ending in `-img` do not accept
fallbacks.

### Sex icons and pictures

Two placeholders render images rather than text and must appear alone in their
text element:

- `[mammal.sex]-img` draws a sex icon (the key must end in `.sex`; set icon
  dimensions with width and height).
- `[media::media]` with `Text type` set to `Picture` renders the record's
  attached images in a grid.

## Custom fields {% #custom-fields %}

A custom field combines placeholders with fixed text, or holds fixed text
alone. In a document template, every text element behaves this way (`Insert
Field` plus typed text). In a record-export preset, select `Add custom field`
in `Edit Fields` or switch a column's `Mapping type` to `Custom field`.

Build the expression segment by segment in the custom field editor:

| Control | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `Add field` | Inserts a field from the picker. |
| `Add text` {% ref id="B" /%} | Inserts fixed text or a separator. |
| `Add conditional text` | Inserts [conditional text](#conditional-text). |
| `Show label` | Adds `#label` on a coded field to print its label instead of its code. |
| `Edit conditional text` | Reopens a conditional text segment for editing. |
| `Move segment up` / `Move segment down` | Reorders segments (written left to right). |
| `Remove segment` | Deletes a segment. |
| `Expression:` | Previews the saved expression string. |
| `Column name` | Sets the output column header. |

Examples of complete custom fields:

```text
[personnel::initial]-[specimen::fieldNumber]
[taxonomy::genus] [taxonomy::specificEpithet]
NAHPU
```

`NAHPU` outputs the same fixed string in every row (useful for an institution
code). A custom field with a `Column name` and no segments writes a blank
column so exported columns align with an external sheet.

Always set a `Column name` (required for Darwin Core and NAHPU namespace
headers). With `table::fieldName` or `fieldName` headers, an unnamed custom
field defaults to its first field key or its fixed text.

Custom field columns output plain text. When you need `Encoded text`, `Date`,
conditional brackets, or indexed list columns, use a `Single field` or
`List field` column instead.

## Conditional output {% #conditional-output %}

A conditional expression checks one or more fields before deciding what to
write. In the template editor, use `Conditional output` on the text toolbar to
create or edit conditionals via dialog. In a tabular preset, pick a conditional
`Value format` on a `Single field` column (its own field is the target).

### Choose a type

| You want to… | Type | Example output |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Bracket a value when another field flags it | `Conditional brackets` | `[82.5]` when weight was estimated |
| Replace a value when another field matches | `Conditional field` | `?` instead of the epithet when ID is uncertain |
| Replace a value based on its own value | `Conditional value` | `Not recorded` when the value is `0` |
| Output standalone text (such as a unit) conditionally | `Conditional text` | ` mm` only after a recorded width |

In the dialog:

{% steps %}

1. Select `Conditional type`.
2. Select `Target field` (the field to bracket or replace). `Conditional text`
   has no target and appends to the element text.
3. Add one or more conditions (`Controlling field`, comparison operator, and
   value). `Conditional value` tests the target itself, so no separate field
   picker appears.
4. For multiple conditions, set `Match logic` to `Any condition (OR)` or
   `All conditions (AND)`.
5. Enter `Replacement text` (or `Text when matched` and optional
   `Text otherwise (optional)` for conditional text). Leave `Replacement text`
   blank to hide the value when matched.

{% /steps %}

### Conditional text (if and else) {% #conditional-text %}

Conditional text writes text based on conditions rather than modifying a target
field—ideal for units or labels that should appear only alongside a value:

```text
[mammalAttribute::testisWidth][[if][mammalAttribute::testisWidth!=""]=>" mm"]]
```

A width of `6.5` prints `6.5 mm`; an empty width prints nothing.

Add `|` and a second quoted string for an else branch:

```text
[[if][mammalAttribute::testisPosition=="0"]=>"scrotal"|"not scrotal"]]
```

Quoted outputs can include placeholders, fallbacks, and `#label`:

```text
[[if][mammalAttribute::testisLength!=""&&mammalAttribute::testisWidth!=""]=>"[mammalAttribute::testisPosition#label], [mammalAttribute::testisLength] x [mammalAttribute::testisWidth] mm"]]
```

- Wrap each output string in double quotes; escape literal quotes as `\"`. A
  `|` inside quotes is treated as ordinary text.
- Without an else branch, non-matching records output nothing.
- Nested conditionals inside quoted output are not evaluated.
- `if` must be lowercase.

### Hide a value unless another field is recorded

Use `Is empty` with an empty replacement. This outputs testis length only when
testis position is recorded:

```text
[[mammalAttribute::testisLength][mammalAttribute::testisPosition==""]=>""]]
```

A conditional hides only its own target. Surrounding text (like a unit or
` x `) still prints unless wrapped in conditional text:

```text
[[mammalAttribute::testisLength][mammalAttribute::testisPosition==""]=>""]][[if][mammalAttribute::testisPosition!=""&&mammalAttribute::testisLength!=""]=>" mm"]]
```

See [Testis size](#testis-size) for the complete combined pattern.

### Worked examples

**Bracket an estimated weight.** A mammal's accuracy note lists measurements
that are estimates. Bracket weight when flagged:

```text
[[mammalAttribute::weight][mammalAttribute::accuracy~="weight"]]
```

Flagged weights print `[82.5]`; precise weights print `82.5`. On
`mammalAttribute::accuracy`, `~=` checks whether the named measurement is
flagged.

**Mark an uncertain identification.** Identification confidence is stored as `0`
(Low), `1` (Medium), or `2` (High), so "not High" is `!="2"`:

```text
[taxonomy::genus] [[taxonomy::specificEpithet][specimen::iDConfidence!="2"]=>"?"]]
```

High confidence prints `Rattus rattus`; Low or Medium prints `Rattus ?`.
Because replacements replace the entire target, append a symbol instead by
following the field with [conditional text](#conditional-text).

`!="2"` does not match a blank confidence field. Include blank records by
adding `Is empty` with `||`:

```text
[[taxonomy::specificEpithet][specimen::iDConfidence=="0"||specimen::iDConfidence=="1"||specimen::iDConfidence==""]=>"?"]]
```

### Rules for conditions

- **Stored values, not labels:** test codes (`specimen::iDConfidence!="2"`,
  `mammalAttribute::testisPosition=="0"`), not display labels.
- **Case-sensitive:** leading and trailing spaces are trimmed, but letter case
  must match.
- **Blank values never match ordinary operators** (including `!=`). Use
  `Is empty` (`==""`) or `Is not empty` (`!=""`).
- **One joiner per expression:** use all `&&` or all `||`, never mixed.
- **Empty target:** uses `No Content Placeholder`, not the replacement text.
- **Full replacement:** replacement text replaces the entire value; an empty
  replacement hides it.
- **Syntax errors print verbatim:** always preview both matching and
  non-matching records.

### Syntax reference

The dialog generates these automatically; use this reference when reading or
editing expressions by hand.

| Symbol | Name | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `[[` … `]]` | Expression delimiters | Open and close a conditional expression. |
| `][` | Target separator | Separates the target field from conditions. |
| `==` | Equals | Matches an exact value. |
| `!=` | Not equals | Matches any non-empty differing value. |
| `~=` | Contains | Matches when the substring appears anywhere in the value. |
| `!=""` | Is not empty | Matches any non-blank value. |
| `==""` | Is empty | Matches blank or missing values. |
| `&&` | All (AND) | Every condition must match. |
| `\|\|` | Any (OR) | At least one condition must match. |
| `"` … `"` | Value quotes | Wrap every comparison value (empty for emptiness checks). |
| `\"`, `\\` | Escapes | Literal quote or backslash inside quotes. |
| `]=>` | Replacement marker | Ends conditions and begins replacement/output text. |
| `if` | Conditional text keyword | Replaces the target so the expression emits text. |
| `\|` | Else separator | Starts the fallback text when conditions do not match. |

Three valid forms (each ending in `]]`; `|"otherwise"` is optional; `~=""` is
invalid):

```text
[[target][conditions]]
[[target][conditions]=>"replacement"]]
[[if][conditions]=>"text"|"otherwise"]]
```

## Text types and their formats {% #text-types-and-their-formats %}

In document templates, `Text type` and `Format` format the rendered value. A
tabular `Single field` column exposes the same formatting via `Value format`.

| Text type | Format options |
| --- | --- |
| `Normal Text` | `Normal`, `Uppercase`, `Lowercase`, `Capitalize` |
| `Picture` | Sized with width and height rather than a format |
| `Markdown` | `Normal`; renders rich text such as narratives |
| `Coordinates` | `Decimal`, `Cardinal Dec`, `DMS`, `DDM` |
| `List Values` | Pipe, comma, semicolon, slash, new line, bulleted, custom separator |
| `Nested List` | `Table` (adds `Header Case`) or `Card list` |
| `Dates` | `YYYY-MM-DD`, `DD-MM-YYYY`, `MM-DD-YYYY`, `DD/MM/YYYY`, `MM/DD/YYYY`, `Month DD, YYYY`, `DD Month YYYY`, `DD Mon YYYY` |
| `Date and Time` | 17 combinations of the date formats above with 24h, 12h, ISO, and time-only outputs |
| `Time` | `24h`, `24h seconds`, `12h`, `12h padded` |
| `Sex` | `Format` and `Missing`, described below |
| `Number` | `Original`, or 0, 1, 2, or 3 decimal places |
| `Encoded Text` | `Default mapping` or `Custom mapping...` |

`Nested List` formats repeated child records (specimen parts, personnel,
collecting methods) and usually benefits from dynamic text sizing.

### Encoded Text: what decodes

Some database fields store numeric codes. `Encoded Text` with `Default mapping`
matches on the end of the field key (so both `mammalAttribute::testisPosition`
and `testisPosition` decode):

| Field key ends with | Code 0 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `::sex` | Male | Female | Unknown | Gynandromorph | Hermaphrodite | Female? | Male? |
| `::iDConfidence` | Low | Medium | High | | | | |
| `mammalAttribute::age` | Adult | Subadult | Juvenile | Unknown | | | |
| `herpAttribute::age` | Adult | Juvenile | Neonate | Metamorph | Unknown | | |
| `::testisPosition` | Scrotal | Abdominal | | | | | |
| `::epididymisAppearance` | Tubular | Partial | Not Tubular | | | | |
| `::vaginaOpening` | Imperforate | Perforate | | | | | |
| `::pubicSymphysis` | Close | Small Open | Open | | | | |
| `::reproductiveStage` | Nulliparous | Primiparous | Multiparous | | | | |
| `::mammaeCondition` | Small | Large | Lactating | | | | |
| `::echolocation` | FM | CF | QCF | None | | | |
| `::ovaryAppearance` | Smooth | Ova minute | At least one ovum ≥ 1 mm dia. | | | | |
| `::oviductAppearance` | Straight | Convoluted | | | | | |
| `::fat` | None | Trace | Light | Moderate | Heavy | Extremely Heavy | |
| `::bodyMolt` | None | Trace | Light | Moderate | Heavy | | |

Boolean flags decode `1` as `Yes` and `0` as `No`: `::broodPatch`,
`::hasBursa`, `::wingIsMolt`, `::tailIsMolt`, `::showBatFields`, and
`::showEchoFields`.

Unlisted keys, non-integer values, and out-of-range codes pass through
unchanged. Use `Custom mapping...` to label fields not covered by the default
table. For sex symbols or letters, use the `Sex` text type; for icons, use
`[…sex]-img`.

### Decode an encoded field {% #decode-an-encoded-field %}

Keep the placeholder unchanged and let `Encoded Text` or `#label` decode it:

- **Document template:** set `Text type` to `Encoded Text`. Each placeholder in
  the element decodes against its own field:
  ```text
  Testes: [mammalAttribute::testisPosition]
  [mammalAttribute::age], [mammalAttribute::testisPosition]
  ```
- **Record-export preset:** use a `Single field` column with `Value format` set
  to `Encoded text`, or in a `Custom field` column append `#label` (or select
  `Show label` on the segment):
  ```text
  [mammalAttribute::testisPosition#label], [mammalAttribute::mammaeCondition#label]
  ```
- **Inline `#label`:** decodes a single placeholder with the default mapping in
  any text type. Place `#label` before any fallback:
  `[mammalAttribute::sex#label??Unknown]`.
- **Custom labels:** in the template editor, choose `Custom mapping...` and
  select `Map encoded values` (starts prefilled from defaults). In a tabular
  preset, enter `custom_map:` under `Advanced` > `Raw format option`:
  ```text
  custom_map:0=Scrotal,1=Abdominal
  ```
  Separate `code=label` pairs with commas (labels cannot contain `,` or `=`;
  unmapped codes stay unchanged). Custom mappings apply to every placeholder in
  the element, so give each custom-mapped field its own element.

Decoding affects display only; conditions still test stored codes and empty
values still use `No Content Placeholder`.

### Sex formatting

| Control | Options |
| --- | --- |
| `Format` | `Symbol (♂/♀)`, `Letter (M/F)`, `Text (Male/Female)` |
| `Missing` | `Unknown`, `N/A`, `None` |

Uncertain determinations retain their question mark in every format: `Female?`,
`F?`, `♀?`, and `Male?`, `M?`, `♂?`.

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | What to check |
| --- | --- |
| Conditional prints as plain text | Syntax error: check for missing `]]`, unquoted values, or mixed `&&` and `\|\|`. |
| Fallback prints `[table::field]` | `No Content Placeholder` is set to `table::field`; switch to `Blank`, `N/A`, `None`, or custom text. |
| Sex icon prints as text | The element must contain only `[…sex]-img`, with a key ending in `.sex`. |
| Record images do not appear | The element must contain only `[media::media]` with `Text type` set to `Picture`. |
| Unexpected custom-field header | Set `Column name`; otherwise it defaults to the first field or fixed text. |
| Coded field prints a number | Use `Encoded Text` / `Encoded text` or `#label`, and verify the code is in the mapping. |
| Condition never matches | Conditions compare stored codes, are case-sensitive, and blank fields only match `Is empty`. |
| Conditional text prints nothing | Add an else branch after `\|` for non-matching records, and ensure `if` is lowercase. |

## Template editor options {% #template-editor-options %}

The reference below applies to the document template editor only {% ref id="E" /%};
record-export presets do not use these controls.

Canvas sizes are in millimetres (`mm`). Stroke widths, font sizes, and padding
are in PDF points (`pt`, 1 pt = 1/72 inch). Colours are stored as `0xAARRGGBB`
and selected with the colour picker.

### Toolbar

| Control | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `Add text` | Places a text element on the canvas. |
| `Add image` | Places a static image from the device. |
| `Add line` | Places a straight rule. |
| `Add shape` | Places a rectangle, ellipse, circle, triangle, or polygon. |
| `Save template` | Saves the template (`Save as...` creates a variation). |
| `Undo` / `Redo` | Steps through edit history. |
| `Template border` | Configures the outer template border. |
| `Show grid` / `Hide grid` | Toggles the alignment grid. |
| `Enable snap` / `Disable snap` | Toggles snapping to the grid and elements. |
| Canvas lock | Locks panning so dragging does not move the canvas. |
| `Select specimen for text preview` | Chooses the record used to populate live preview placeholders. |
| `Template settings` {% ref id="D" /%} | Name, description, side count, and template size. |
| `Preset template` {% ref id="A" /%} | Loads a bundled starting template. |
| `Zoom in` / `Zoom out` | Scales canvas view only (does not affect PDF size). |
| `1 sided` / `Front` / `Back` | Switches side mode and active side. |
| Mirror | Mirrors a side for folded tags. |

### Text element options

#### Content

| Option | Values | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Text | Text, placeholders, conditionals | Element content. |
| `Text type` | See table above | Selects value formatting category. |
| `Format` | Depends on `Text type` | Specific format within that category. |
| `No Content Placeholder` | Blank, `table::field`, `N/A`, `None`, custom | Writes `??` fallback. |
| `Conditional output` | Brackets, field, value, text | Writes `[[ … ]]` or `[[if] … ]]` expressions. |
| `Find and replace` | — | Edits element text in place. |
| Replacement rules | Pattern, replacement, match type, case sensitivity | Rewrites values after formatting. |
| `Map encoded values` | Default or custom mapping | Maps stored codes to labels for `Encoded Text`. |

#### Type and style

| Option | Values |
| --- | --- |
| `Font` | Bundled and installed fonts (missing fonts are marked `(not installed)`) |
| Font size | Points, with step buttons |
| `Bold`, `Italic`, `Underline`, `Strikethrough` | On or off |
| Alignment | `Align left`, `Align center`, `Align right` |
| Case | `Normal`, `Uppercase`, `Lowercase`, `Capitalize` |
| Text colour | Colour picker |

#### Box and placement

| Option | Values | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Position | X and Y in `mm` | Measured from the template's top-left corner. |
| Max width | `mm` | Wraps text at this width (unset = no wrapping). |
| Height | `mm` | Bounds box height. |
| Padding | `pt` | Space inside the box around text. |
| Rotation | `0–359°` | Whole degrees. |
| Background colour | Colour or none | — |
| Border colour, width, stroke | Colour, `pt`, `solid` / `dashed` / `dotted` / `double` | — |
| Corner radius | `pt` | Rounds box corners. |
| Dynamic sizing | On or off | Lets the box grow with content; pair with `Auto-fill page`. |
| Stacking | `Bring to front`, `Bring forward`, `Send backward`, `Send to back` | — |
| Lock | On or off | Prevents dragging or resizing. |
| Visible | On or off | Hidden elements stay saved but do not print. |

#### QR code

Convert a text element into a scannable QR code:

| Option | Values |
| --- | --- |
| QR code | On or off |
| Size | `mm` |
| Background colour | Colour picker |
| Shape | `Square` or `Circle` |

The QR payload keeps the raw formatted value—including trailing `.0` values
that printed text drops—so scanned values match stored values exactly.

#### Picture

| Option | Values |
| --- | --- |
| Width, height | `mm` |

Only a bare `[media::media]` or `[media]` element resolves to record images;
mixing text with the placeholder disables image rendering.

### Image, line, and shape options

Static images, lines, and shapes are decorative and carry no record data:

| Element | Options |
| --- | --- |
| Image | Image path, position, width, height, rotation, stacking, lock, visibility |
| Line | Position, length, rotation, thickness (`pt`), colour, stroke style, stacking, lock, visibility |
| Shape | Shape type (`rect`, `ellipse`, `circle`, `triangle`, `polygon` with side count), position, width, height, rotation, stroke thickness/colour/style, fill colour or `Clear fill`, stacking, lock, visibility |

Stroke styles for lines and shapes are `solid`, `dashed`, `dotted`, and
`double`. Static image elements store a path rather than embedding the picture;
templates transferred to another device ask for the image again there.

### Template options

| Option | Values | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Template name` | Text | Must be unique; renaming updates all print layouts referencing it. |
| `Description` | Text (up to 80 characters) | Optional. |
| `Record type` | `Specimen`, `Specimen parts`, `Symbionts`, `Site`, `Collecting event`, `Narrative`, `No records` | Determines available fields and records. |
| Side count | `1 sided` or `2 sided` | One-sided mode keeps the Back design saved without printing it. |
| Width, height | `mm` | Size of one block, not the sheet. |
| Template border | `solid`, `dashed`, `dotted`, `double line`; width (`pt`); colour | — |

Print options stored with a template cover duplex, front/back mirroring, page
size, rows/columns per page, page padding, and document padding. A print-layout
preset overrides these for the exported PDF; see
[Create a print-layout preset](../export-documents#create-a-print-layout-preset).
